tore identity is a configuration detail at execution time. |\n\n## Conditional Branches\n\nE001 has exactly two bounded outcomes:\n\n- **Branch A — MinIO cleared for redistribution**: productize MinIO (E006–E009 chain).\n- **Branch B — AGPL terms cannot be satisfied**: productize the Apache-2.0 fallback\n  (SeaweedFS); the strategy marks this acceptable but it restarts image productization,\n  so the full onboarding chain is replicated per branch.\n\nBranch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=E001` (also in `dependencies`), and\n`gate_failure_impact.action=remove` (if the other outcome holds, this branch's work is\nnot executed — the mirror branch performs the equivalent chain). Main-plan epics never\ndepend on branch epics; work that depends on the *outcome* depends on E001 itself.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n|-----|----------|---------|\n| HLR-1 (legal review of AGPL redistribution, documented) | P0 | E001 |\n| HLR-2 (admin-enableable bundled store via Platform Operator, productized images, upgrade lifecycle) | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E006..E009, BRANCH-B-E006..E009 |\n| HLR-3 (Pipelines and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store) | P1 | E003 (Pipelines), E004 (model serving) |\n| HLR-4 (documentation: enablement, sizing, support boundary) | P2 | E005 |\n\nFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- The bundled object store (MinIO / SeaweedFS) has no canonical RHAI Jira component —\n  it is a new component with no architecture context file. All store-productization\n  epics (E001, E002, and both branches) are assigned the single most-relevant canonical\n  name **Platform Operator**, since the store ships exclusively through the Platform\n  Operator enablement surface. This span is noted here per the component-name constraint.\n- \"Model serving\" in HLR-3 is not in the Affected Components list; mapped to the\n  canonical component **Serving Runtimes**.