esent.\n- When enabled, the store is running and exposes an S3-compatible endpoint usable by\n  Data Science Pipelines and model serving.\n- The enablement is opt-in (off by default) and a documented disable/rollback path\n  exists; clusters with customer-provided storage continue to work unchanged.\n- The bundled store is managed across a platform upgrade (image updates reconciled\n  without manual intervention).\n- A pinned image digest of the productized store is available at packaging time and is\n  referenced by the operator's distribution artifacts (this is a configuration\n  reference; the image productization work proceeds in parallel).\n- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are implemented in the operator\n  integration.\n- The capability is technically reviewed against the implementation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Gated by the legal clearance investigation: if the AGPL candidate cannot be cleared,\n  the bundled image reference and any store-specific validation are re-targeted to the\n  Apache-2.0 fallback; the enablement surface itself is unchanged.\n- Today field teams install upstream MinIO ad hoc, unsupported and invisible to the\n  platform; this epic replaces that workaround with a supported path, so the opt-in\n  default and rollback path above are first-class scope, not afterthoughts.\n- No architecture context file exists for the Platform Operator component; claims about\n  its enablement mechanisms could not be validated against architecture context.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42152,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35faa3c50ce9d5b","agent_id":"a4eb990e8b7c5352b","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"b0