ng guidance, and the\n  supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage, matching the topics\n  in the Scope outline.\n- The documentation accurately reflects the shipped implementation (which store is\n  bundled, the enablement mechanism, the upgrade behavior) — technically reviewed\n  against the implementation by the owning engineers.\n- The boundary documentation explicitly states the strategy's out-of-scope items\n  (customer-provided S3 in connected environments is not replaced; no data migration\n  tooling between stores).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the\n  supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The documented store identity (the cleared candidate vs the Apache-2.0 fallback)\n  follows the legal clearance outcome; documentation drafting starts only after the\n  implementation epics complete.\n- Priority is derived from the strategy-level priority (Major → P1) per the\n  docs-authoring priority exception, even though HLR-4 is P2.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44207,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35faa3c50ce9d5b","agent_id":"a4eb990e8b7c5352b","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"3e9c8eea-a3dc-4fbe-83f8-722775ca7df9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:19:42.165Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9012"}
