erator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are satisfied by the shipped image.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, MinIO branch).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Depends on upstream MinIO release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing is\n  tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects MinIO.\n  If the AGPL terms cannot be satisfied, this work restarts against the Apache-2.0\n  fallback (SeaweedFS).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46643,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35faa3c50ce9d5b","agent_id":"a4eb990e8b7c5352b","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"130d80c2-0710-4e1d-b6c9-dc0898b50c4f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:20:26.291Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9012"}
