 of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Depends on upstream SeaweedFS release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing\n  is tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n- SeaweedFS is a less-proven fallback than the original candidate; functional\n  validation of the S3-compatible surface against Data Science Pipelines and model\n  serving workloads is folded into the acceptance criteria of the consuming epics.\n- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome rejects the\n  AGPL candidate.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49113,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35faa3c50ce9d5b","agent_id":"a4eb990e8b7c5352b","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"25037b59-2ea5-41ef-80ed-4f185cbf2ed1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:21:10.887Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9012"}
