{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b242fcbef2a7b7fa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n3\ttitle: Legal clearance for redistributing the AGPL-3.0 candidate object store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Legal clearance for redistributing the AGPL-3.0 candidate object store\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the leading S3-compatible object store candidate,\n30\tMinIO (AGPL-3.0), can be redistributed as part of the platform's distribution model,\n31\tincluding the derivative-work posture for integrating it with the Platform Operator\n32\t(bundling, OLM-managed deployment, and productized images). The outcome is a documented\n33\tlegal decision that gates all shipping work for the bundled-store strategy and selects\n34\twhich upstream is productized: MinIO if the terms are cleared, or the Apache-2.0\n35\tfallback (e.g. SeaweedFS) if they are not.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Legal analysis of AGPL-3.0 redistribution terms for the candidate store under the\n40\t  platform's distribution model (disconnected/install-bundle redistribution of\n41\t  container images).\n42\t- Derivative-work posture for operator integration: whether deploying, configuring, and\n43\t  productizing the store via the Platform Operator creates derivative-work obligations.\n44\t- A documented decision record covering both questions, filed with the strategy.\n45\t- If the terms cannot be satisfied: confirmation that the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate\n46\t  is acceptable and a recommendation to restart image productization against it.\n47\t- Identification of any conditions or restrictions attached to clearance (attribution\n48\t  requirements, aggregation boundaries, patch-disclosure obligations) that downstream\n49\t  productization and packaging work must honor.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A written legal decision exists that states, pass/fail, whether the AGPL-3.0\n54\t  candidate can be redistributed in the platform's distribution model.\n55\t- The decision documents the derivative-work posture for operator integration.\n56\t- Any conditions attached to clearance are enumerated concretely enough for the\n57\t  productization and packaging work to implement them.\n58\t- If clearance is denied, the decision record names the fallback candidate and states\n59\t  that image productization restarts against it.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store (MinIO,\n64\t  AGPL-3.0) is completed and documented, including the derivative-work posture for\n65\t  operator integration.\n66\t\n67\t## Risks / Notes\n68\t\n69\t- The gating question is a legal/governance decision made by counsel, not an\n70\t  engineering finding; engineering supports the analysis with distribution-model facts\n71\t  (what is shipped, how the operator deploys and configures the store) but does not\n72\t  decide. Turnaround is outside engineering control.\n73\t- The strategy's open question explicitly bounds the outcome to two possibilities\n74\t  (MinIO cleared, or Apache-2.0 fallback), which drives the conditional productization\n75\t  branches recorded in the decomposition summary.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"4b71abd8-8a