{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9423508addf73cfa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E002\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the AGPL candidate is not cleared, re-target the bundled image\n15\t    reference and store-specific validation to the Apache-2.0 fallback store; the\n16\t    enablement surface itself is store-agnostic\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: -1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDeliver the administrator-facing capability to enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible\n39\tobject store through the Platform Operator, so that disconnected and PoC clusters get\n40\tsupported, patched storage for pipelines and model serving without customer-provided S3.\n41\tThe store is opt-in, deployed from productized images, and managed through the platform\n42\tupgrade lifecycle.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- An opt-in enablement mechanism in the Platform Operator that deploys the bundled\n47\t  S3-compatible object store (the specific upstream — the AGPL candidate or the\n48\t  Apache-2.0 fallback — is fixed by the legal clearance decision; this epic's enablement\n49\t  surface is store-agnostic and consumes the store as a productized image reference).\n50\t- Deployment of the store with a cluster-internal S3 endpoint that Data Science\n51\t  Pipelines and model serving can target.\n52\t- Upgrade lifecycle handling: the operator reconciles the bundled store across platform\n53\t  upgrades, including image updates.\n54\t- A disable/rollback path: administrators can turn the bundled store off, and clusters\n55\t  using customer-provided S3 are unaffected (enablement is opt-in and defaults to off).\n56\t- Packaging of the productized store image reference (e.g. as a pinned image digest) in\n57\t  the operator's distribution artifacts, honoring any conditions attached to the legal\n58\t  clearance.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- An administrator can enable the bundled S3-compatible object store through the\n63\t  Platform Operator on a disconnected cluster, with no customer-provided S3 present.\n64\t- When enabled, the store is running and exposes an S3-compatible endpoint usable by\n65\t  Data Science Pipelines and model serving.\n66\t- The enablement is opt-in (off by default) and a documented disable/rollback path\n67\t  exists; clusters with customer-provided storage continue to work unchanged.\n68\t- The bundled store is managed across a platform upgrade (image updates reconciled\n69\t  without manual intervention).\n70\t- A pinned image digest of the productized store is available at packaging time and is\n71\t  referenced by the operator's distribution artifacts (this is a configuration\n72\t  reference; the image productization work proceeds in parallel).\n73\t- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are implemented in the operator\n74\t  integration.\n75\t- The capability is technically reviewed against the implementation.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n80\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- Gated by the legal clearance investigation: if the AGPL candidate cannot be cleared,\n85\t  the bundled image reference and any store-specific validation are re-targeted to the\n86\t  Apache-2.0 fallback; the enablement surface itself is unchanged.\n87\t- Today field teams install upstream MinIO ad hoc, unsupported and invisible to the\n88\t  platform; this epic replaces that workaround with a supported path, so the opt-in\n89\t  default and rollback path above are first-class scope, not afterthoughts.\n90\t- No architecture context file exists for the Platform Operator component; claims about\n91\t  its enablement mechanisms could not be validated against architecture context.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"4f5cfa7e-6976-44a4-859f-440c7d545990","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:25:53.250Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9423508addf73cfa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
