{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbc2bfb148a9ffa2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E003\n3\ttitle: Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Data Science Pipelines\n6\tteam: RHOAI Pipelines\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMake Data Science Pipelines target the bundled S3-compatible object store by default\n34\twhen it is enabled, so that pipeline artifact storage works on disconnected clusters\n35\twithout manual endpoint configuration. Today the platform's pipelines depend on\n36\tS3-compatible object storage for artifacts (per the Data Science Pipelines architecture\n37\tcontext), which disconnected customers frequently lack.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Default artifact-storage connection configuration in the Data Science Pipelines\n42\t  operator so that, when the bundled store is enabled on a cluster, pipeline\n43\t  applications use it without administrators hand-configuring endpoints or credentials.\n44\t- Explicitly configured customer-provided S3 continues to take precedence over the\n45\t  bundled-store default (no regression for connected environments).\n46\t- Coordination contract: the default resolves the bundled store's endpoint through the\n47\t  convention established by the Platform Operator enablement capability (an endpoint\n48\t  reference, not a build-time artifact).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- On a cluster where the bundled store is enabled, a Data Science Pipelines application\n53\t  can be created and run with zero manual endpoint or credential configuration for\n54\t  artifact storage.\n55\t- Where an administrator has explicitly configured customer-provided S3, that\n56\t  configuration is honored and the bundled-store default does not override it.\n57\t- Pipeline runs storing artifacts in the bundled store surface correctly in the\n58\t  Dashboard with no Dashboard code changes (passive-component validation — the\n59\t  Dashboard reads pipeline-run CRs and owns no data plane).\n60\t- The defaulting behavior is covered by automated tests.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-3 (P1): Data Science Pipelines and model serving connection defaults can target\n65\t  the bundled store without manual endpoint configuration (Data Science Pipelines\n66\t  portion).\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- The bundled-store endpoint is a configuration reference resolved at execution time;\n71\t  this work proceeds in parallel with the Platform Operator enablement capability and\n72\t  is gated by the acceptance criterion above rather than a hard ordering.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"17c3b822-47ae-45cb-9b61-dccb6c35dc30","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:25:57.022Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbc2bfb148a9ffa2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
