le dependencies\n50\t  found in the image build.\n51\t- Remediation recommendations for any findings (dependency replacement, exclusion, or\n52\t  additional clearance) handed to the image productization work.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A license scan report exists covering MinIO and the complete transitive dependency\n57\t  set of the productized store image.\n58\t- Every dependency in the shipped image is classified as policy-compliant, or has a\n59\t  documented remediation carried into the image productization work.\n60\t- Scan findings that require legal interpretation are escalated and tracked to\n61\t  resolution.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n66\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n67\t  (supported/productized-images portion, MinIO branch).\n68\t\n69\t## Risks / Notes\n70\t\n71\t- Findings requiring legal sign-off introduce a human review gate; the scan itself is\n72\t  automated, but interpretation of edge-case licenses is not.\n73\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects MinIO.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"b4224ada-4abc-48d3-a31d-bfae29c369ac","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:26:04.452Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86c77c9594d0c707","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
