{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a8f48f25db54bc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E007\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the AGPL candidate is not cleared, image productization restarts\n17\t    against the Apache-2.0 fallback store (SeaweedFS), per the strategy open question\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: -1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: -1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tProductize the MinIO container image for bundling: a supported, rebuildable image built\n39\tfrom the midstream repository through Konflux, with the version/upgrade policy that the\n40\tPlatform Operator's upgrade lifecycle relies on. This work is conditional on the legal\n41\tclearance outcome selecting MinIO as the bundled store.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Container image productization for the store: build hardening, image configuration,\n46\t  and version pinning aligned with the cleared upstream version.\n47\t- Upgrade lifecycle support: a defined policy for tracking and ingesting upstream MinIO\n48\t  releases (including security patches) into the productized image, so bundled stores\n49\t  stay supported and patched — the explicit gap left by today's ad hoc field installs.\n50\t- Incorporation of any remediations required by the license validation of the image's\n51\t  transitive dependencies, and of any conditions attached to the legal clearance.\n52\t- A pinned image digest consumable as a configuration reference by the Platform\n53\t  Operator packaging.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A productized MinIO container image builds from the midstream repository with the\n58\t  Konflux build pipeline green.\n59\t- The image's transitive-dependency license findings are resolved or documented as\n60\t  cleared.\n61\t- The upgrade policy is implemented: a new upstream MinIO release (including security\n62\t  patches) can be ingested into a new productized image through the standard pipeline.\n63\t- A pinned image digest of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n64\t  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n65\t  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n66\t- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are satisfied by the shipped image.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n71\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n72\t  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, MinIO branch).\n73\t\n74\t## Risks / Notes\n75\t\n76\t- Depends on upstream MinIO release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing is\n77\t  tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n78\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects MinIO.\n79\t  If the AGPL terms cannot be satisfied, this work restarts against the Apache-2.0\n80\t  fallback (SeaweedFS).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64