m repositories.\n50\t- Seed the repository with build metadata sufficient for later Konflux onboarding and\n51\t  image builds (Dockerfile/container build definition for the store image, including\n52\t  the S3-compatible gateway/server configuration used for the bundled deployment).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A midstream SeaweedFS repository exists under opendatahub.io containing the upstream\n57\t  sources at a pinned version.\n58\t- The repository follows the organization's midstream conventions (branching, license\n59\t  and provenance files, upstream-sync process documented).\n60\t- A container build definition for the store image builds locally from the repository.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n65\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n66\t  (productized-images portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome rejects the\n71\t  AGPL candidate. Selecting SeaweedFS restarts image productization, per the strategy's\n72\t  open question — the onboarding, scanning, pipeline, and image work all re-run against\n73\t  the new upstream.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0ddfef4d311b9","agent_id":"a3c3c25481f8c080e","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"4b9f3ceb-b0f3-401d-8813-b4b05b7bcc83","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:26:11.380Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d2af45d9d2421e6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
