{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8150f1d234655b4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Productized SeaweedFS container image with upgrade lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E007\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the AGPL candidate is cleared, this branch is not executed;\n17\t    MinIO image productization runs instead\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: -1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: -1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productized SeaweedFS container image with upgrade lifecycle\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tProductize the SeaweedFS container image for bundling: a supported, rebuildable image\n39\tbuilt from the midstream repository through Konflux, with the version/upgrade policy\n40\tthat the Platform Operator's upgrade lifecycle relies on. This work is conditional on\n41\tthe legal clearance outcome selecting the Apache-2.0 fallback as the bundled store.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Container image productization for the store: build hardening, image configuration\n46\t  (including the S3-compatible server configuration used for the bundled deployment),\n47\t  and version pinning aligned with the selected upstream version.\n48\t- Upgrade lifecycle support: a defined policy for tracking and ingesting upstream\n49\t  SeaweedFS releases (including security patches) into the productized image, so\n50\t  bundled stores stay supported and patched — the explicit gap left by today's ad hoc\n51\t  field installs.\n52\t- Incorporation of any remediations required by the license validation of the image's\n53\t  transitive dependencies.\n54\t- A pinned image digest consumable as a configuration reference by the Platform\n55\t  Operator packaging.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A productized SeaweedFS container image builds from the midstream repository with the\n60\t  Konflux build pipeline green.\n61\t- The image's transitive-dependency license findings are resolved or documented as\n62\t  cleared.\n63\t- The upgrade policy is implemented: a new upstream SeaweedFS release (including\n64\t  security patches) can be ingested into a new productized image through the standard\n65\t  pipeline.\n66\t- A pinned image digest of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n67\t  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n68\t  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n73\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n74\t  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Depends on upstream SeaweedFS release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing\n79\t  is tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n80\t- SeaweedFS is a less-proven fallback than the original candidate; functional\n81\t  validation of the S3-compatible surface against Data Science Pipelines and model\n82\t  serving workloads is folded into the acceptance criteria of the consuming epics.\n83\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome rejects the\n84\t  AGPL candidate.\n85\t"}]},"