 supported and patched — the explicit gap left by today's ad hoc field installs.\n50\t- Incorporation of any remediations required by the license validation of the image's\n51\t  transitive dependencies, and of any conditions attached to the legal clearance.\n52\t- A pinned image digest consumable as a configuration reference by the Platform\n53\t  Operator packaging.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A productized MinIO container image builds from the midstream repository with the\n58\t  Konflux build pipeline green.\n59\t- The image's transitive-dependency license findings are resolved or documented as\n60\t  cleared.\n61\t- The upgrade policy is implemented: a new upstream MinIO release (including security\n62\t  patches) can be ingested into a new productized image through the standard pipeline.\n63\t- A pinned image digest of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n64\t  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n65\t  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n66\t- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are satisfied by the shipped image.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n71\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n72\t  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, MinIO branch).\n73\t\n74\t## Risks / Notes\n75\t\n76\t- Depends on upstream MinIO release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing is\n77\t  tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n78\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects MinIO.\n79\t  If the AGPL terms cannot be satisfied, this work restarts against the Apache-2.0\n80\t  fallback (SeaweedFS).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9605b1b4cb9a760f","agent_id":"a8de1ef08bb0f2983","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64