| Rule 3 / HLR-1 | Legal clearance is a genuine unknown whose outcome (MinIO vs Apache-2.0 fallback) changes what ships; HLR-1 states it blocks all shipping work. True gate (`rewrite`: enablement re-targets to the fallback store). |\n71\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic. |\n72\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n73\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n74\t| E001 → A/B-E006, E001 → A/B-E007 | Rule 3 + Rule 20 | The onboarding chain is branch-conditional: the midstream repo, license scan, and image differ per upstream. repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation run in parallel (Rule 7) once the store is selected. |\n75\t| A/B-E006 → A/B-E008 | Rule 5 | Konflux onboarding needs the midstream repo to exist. |\n76\t| A/B-E007 → A/B-E009 | Rule 9 | License validation gates general implementation: if licenses fail, dependencies change and the approach changes. |\n77\t| (none) A/B-E008 → A/B-E009 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding ∥ general implementation — deliberately NO edge in either direction; the \"build pipeline green\" AC on the image epic enforces the coupling. |\n78\t\n79\t### Deliberate non-edges\n80\t\n81\t| Non-edge | Rule | Rationale |\n82\t|----------|------|-----------|\n83\t| productized image ↛ E002 (operator enablement) | Rule 13 | The productized store image digest consumed by operator packaging/OLM is a **configuration reference**, not a build-against artifact. E002 carries a \"pinned image digest of the productized store available\" AC; the digest is filled in at execution time and the epics run in parallel. |\n84\t| E002 ↛ E003 / E004 | Rule 13 / Rule 15 | The bundled store endpoint that Pipelines and model-serving defaults target is a configuration reference (endpoint URL), not a build-against artifact. Defaults work is store-agnostic (S3-compatible API either way), lives in different repos, and carries \"bundled store endpoint available when enabled\" AC gates instead of DAG edges. |\n85\t| E001 ↛ E003 / E004 | Step 3 decision rule | The legal outcome does not change what the defaults epics build (both candidate stores expose the same S3-compatible API and the same operator-managed endpoint pattern), so they are not gated; the store identity is a configuration detail at execution time. |\n86\t\n87\t## Conditional Branches\n88\t\n89\tE001 has exactly two bounded outcomes:\n90\t\n91\t- **Branch A — MinIO cleared for redistribution**: productize MinIO (E006–E009 chain).\n92\t- **Branch B — AGPL terms cannot be satisfied**: productize the Apache-2.0 fallback\n93\t  (SeaweedFS); the strategy marks this acceptable but it restarts image productization,\n94\t  so the full onboarding chain is replicated per branch.\n95\t\n96\tBranch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=E001` (also in `dependencies`), and\n97\t`gate_failure_impact.action=remove` (if the other outcome holds, this branch's work is\n98\tnot executed — the mirror branch performs the equivalent chain). Main-plan epics never\n99\tdepend on branch epics; work that depends on the *outcome* depends on E001 itself.\n100\t\n101\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n102\t\n103\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n104\t|-----|----------|---------|\n105\t| HLR-1 (legal review of AGPL redistribution, documented) | P0 | E001 |\n106\t| HLR-2 (admin-enableable bundled store via Platform Operator, productized images, upgrade lifecycle) | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E006..E009, BRANCH-B-E006..E009 |\n107\t| HLR-3 (Pipelines and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store) | P1 | E003 (Pipelines), E004 (model serving) |\n108\t| HLR-4 (documentation: enablement, sizing, support boundary) | P2 | E005 |\n109\t\n110\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n111\t\n112\t## Component Mapping Notes\n113\t\n114\t- The bundled object store (MinIO / SeaweedFS) has no canonical RHAI Jira component —\n115\t  it is a new component with no architecture context file. All store-productization\n116\t  epics (E001, E002, and both branches) are assigned the single most-relevant canonical\n117\t  name **Platform Operator**, since the store ships exclusively through the Platform\n118\t  Operator enablement surface. This span is noted here per the component-name constraint.\n119\t- \"Model serving\" in HLR-3 is not in the Affected Components list; mapped to the\n120\t  canonical component **Serving Runtimes**.\n121\t- **Dashboard** is listed in Affected Components but no HLR requires Dashboard changes\n122\t  and the store is administrator-facing infrastructure (the Dashboard owns no data plane\n123\t  and reads only Kubernetes CRs per its architecture context). Classified as **passive**\n124\t  (no code changes, keep working): validation is an acceptance criterion on the Data\n125\t  Science Pipelines defaults epic — pipeline runs storing artifacts in the bundled store\n126\t  must continue to surface correctly in the Dashboard.\n127\t\n128\t## Tiered Delivery\n129\t\n130\tNot applied as an external-timing tier split. The legal review (E001) is a hard gate\n131\twith a bounded outcome, modeled as conditional branches rather than a timing tier.\n132\tWithin each branch, Konflux onboarding and image productization run in parallel (Rule 10)\n133\tso the pipeline is ready as soon as the image builds stabilize.\n134\t\n135\t## Health Warnings\n136\t\n137\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, and Affected\n138\t   Components is a bare list without change/owner detail. Teams were inferred —\n139\t   RHOAI Pipelines and RHOAI Dashboard from architecture context owning-team fields;\n140\t   RHOAI Platform Operator, RHOAI Model Serving, and RHOAI Documentation inferred from\n141\t   component names. Verify with the strategy author.\n142\t2. **No architecture context for Platform Operator or Serving Runtimes**: only Dashboard\n143\t   and Data Science Pipelines have architecture context files. Claims about those\n144\t   components could not be validated against architecture context; the architecture\n145\t   signal on the corresponding epics is scored unfavorably.\n146\t3. **Legal review is a human/governance gate**: E001's gating question is a legal\n147\t   decision (AGPL-3.0 redistribution and derivative-work posture) that AI tooling can\n148\t   support with research but cannot resolve; its investigation signals route it to a\n149\t   person. Turnaround is outside engineering control.\n150\t4. **Stranded-work risk**: E003/E004 (defaults) are intentionally not gated by E001\n151\t   because the strategy marks the SeaweedFS fallback as acceptable, so a bundled store\n152\t   ships in every bounded outcome. If both candidates were ultimately unshippable, the\n153\t   defaults work would be stranded — accepted risk, flagged for the reviewer.\n154\t5. **Dashboard ambiguity**: see Component Mapping Notes — passive classification is an\n155\t   interpretation; if the strategy author intended a Dashboard configuration/status\n156\t   surface for the bundled store, a Dashboard epic should be added.\n157\t\n158\t## Triage\n159\t\n160\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only): the strategy spans multiple\n161\tcomponents and architecturally distinct work streams (legal investigation, new-component\n162\tonboarding chain, operator enablement, per-component defaults, substantive documentation\n163\tauthoring), and contains a genuine unknown (AGPL clearance) that changes which epics exist.\n164\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9605b1b4cb9a760f","agent_id":"a8de1ef08bb0f2983","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"180bc310-4107-4e51-9326-b89939ed57f0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:30:17.309Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-868b4aba4e83c15a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
