{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbd95cdf8ba1822","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012 (Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy priority: Major. The strategy is NOT below threshold (four components, multiple\n13\twork streams: legal investigation, image productization chain, operator enablement,\n14\tcomponent defaults, documentation) and NOT docs-only, so it proceeds through full\n15\tdecomposition.\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n20\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n21\t| E001 | Legal clearance for redistributing the AGPL-3.0 candidate object store | Investigation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n22\t| E002 | Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n23\t| E003 | Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n24\t| E004 | Model serving storage defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Model Serving | P1 |\n25\t| E005 | Bundled object store documentation (enablement, sizing, support boundary) | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n26\t| BRANCH-A-E006 | Midstream onboarding of the MinIO repository under opendatahub.io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n27\t| BRANCH-A-E007 | License scan of MinIO and its transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n28\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the MinIO midstream repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n29\t| BRANCH-A-E009 | Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n30\t| BRANCH-B-E006 | Midstream onboarding of the SeaweedFS repository under opendatahub.io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n31\t| BRANCH-B-E007 | License scan of SeaweedFS and its transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n32\t| BRANCH-B-E008 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the SeaweedFS midstream repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n33\t| BRANCH-B-E009 | Productized SeaweedFS container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n34\t\n35\tMain plan: E001–E005 (5 epics). Branch epics are conditional alternatives attached to\n36\tthe E001 investigation outcome, not standalone Jira issues.\n37\t\n38\t## Dependency DAG\n39\t\n40\t```mermaid\n41\tgraph TD\n42\t    E001[\"E001 Legal clearance (Investigation)\"]\n43\t    E002[\"E002 Platform Operator enablement\"]\n44\t    E003[\"E003 Pipelines connection defaults\"]\n45\t    E004[\"E004 Model serving storage defaults\"]\n46\t    E005[\"E005 Documentation\"]\n47\t    E001 --> E002\n48\t    E002 --> E005\n49\t    E003 --> E005\n50\t    E004 --> E005\n51\t\n52\t    subgraph Branch A — MinIO cleared\n53\t        AE006[\"A-E006 repo-onboarding\"] --> AE008[\"A-E008 konflux-onboarding\"]\n54\t        AE006 --> AE009[\"A-E009 productized image\"]\n55\t        AE007[\"A-E007 license-validation\"] --> AE009\n56\t    end\n57\t    E001 --> AE006\n58\t    E001 --> AE007\n59\t\n60\t    subgraph Branch B — AGPL not satisfiable, SeaweedFS fallback\n61\t        BE006[\"B-E006 repo-onboarding\"] --> BE008[\"B-E008 konflux-onboarding\"]\n62\t        BE006 --> BE009[\"B-E009 productized image\"]\n63\t        BE007[\"B-E007 license-validation\"] --> BE009\n64\t    end\n65\t    E001 --> BE006\n66\t    E001 --> BE007\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t## DAG Justification\n70\t\n71\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n72\t|------|------|-----------|\n73\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 / HLR-1 | Legal clearance is a genuine unknown whose outcome (MinIO vs Apache-2.0 fallback) changes what ships; HLR-1 states it blocks all shipping work. True gate (`rewrite`: enablement re-targets to the fallback store). |\n74\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic. |\n75\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n76\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n77\t| E001 → A/B-E006, E001 → A/B-E007 | Rule 3 + Rule 20 | The onboarding chain is branch-conditional: the midstream repo, license scan, and image differ per upstream. repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation run in parallel (Rule 7) once the store is selected. |\n78\t| A/B-E006 → A/B-E008 | Rule 5 | Konflux onboarding needs the midstream repo to exist. |\n79\t| A/B-E006 → A/B-E009 | Rule 6 | repo-onboarding precedes the general implementation of the onboarded component (code needs repo): the productized image builds from the midstream repository created by the repo-onboarding epic. |\n80\t| A/B-E007 → A/B-E009 | Rule 9 | License validation gates general implementation: if licenses fail, dependencies change and the approach changes. |\n81\t| (none) A/B-E008 → A/B-E009 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding ∥ general implementation — deliberately NO edge in either direction; the \"build pipeline green\" AC on the image epic enforces the coupling. |\n82\t\n83\t### Deliberate non-edges\n84\t\n85\t| Non-edge | Rule | Rationale |\n86\t|----------|------|-----------|\n87\t| productized image ↛ E002 (operator enablement) | Rule 13 | The productized store image digest consumed by operator packaging/OLM is a **configuration reference**, not a build-against artifact. E002 carries a \"pinned image digest of the productized store available\" AC; the digest is filled in at execution time and the epics run in parallel. |\n88\t| E002 ↛ E003 / E004 | Rule 13 / Rule 15 | The bundled store endpoint that Pipelines and model-serving defaults target is a configuration reference (endpoint URL), not a build-against artifact. Defaults work is store-agnostic (S3-compatible API either way), lives in different repos, and carries \"bundled store endpoint available when enabled\" AC gates instead of DAG edges. |\n89\t| E001 ↛ E003 / E004 | Step 3 decision rule | The legal outcome does not change what the defaults epics build (both candidate stores expose the same S3-compatible API and the same operator-managed endpoint pattern), so they are not gated; the store identity is a configuration detail at execution time. |\n90\t\n91\t## Conditional Branches\n92\t\n93\tE001 has exactly two bounded outcomes:\n94\t\n95\t- **Branch A — MinIO cleared for redistribution**: productize MinIO (E006–E009 chain).\n96\t- **Branch B — AGPL terms cannot be satisfied**: productize the Apache-2.0 fallback\n97\t  (SeaweedFS); the strategy marks this acceptable but it restarts image productization,\n98\t  so the full onboarding chain is replicated per branch.\n99\t\n100\tBranch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=E001` (also in `dependencies`), and\n101\t`gate_failure_impact.action=remove` (if the other outcome holds, this branch's work is\n102\tnot executed — the mirror branch performs the equivalent chain). Main-plan epics never\n103\tdepend on branch epics; work that depends on the *outcome* depends on E001 itself.\n104\t\n105\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n106\t\n107\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n108\t|-----|----------|---------|\n109\t| HLR-1 (legal review of AGPL redistribution, documented) | P0 | E001 |\n110\t| HLR-2 (admin-enableable bundled store via Platform Operator, productized images, upgrade lifecycle) | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E006..E009, BRANCH-B-E006..E009 |\n111\t| HLR-3 (Pipelines and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store) | P1 | E003 (Pipelines), E004 (model serving) |\n112\t| HLR-4 (documentation: enablement, sizing, support boundary) | P2 | E005 |\n113\t\n114\tFull coverage: every