cumentation inferred from\n145\t   component names. Verify with the strategy author.\n146\t2. **No architecture context for Platform Operator or Serving Runtimes**: only Dashboard\n147\t   and Data Science Pipelines have architecture context files. Claims about those\n148\t   components could not be validated against architecture context; the architecture\n149\t   signal on the corresponding epics is scored unfavorably.\n150\t3. **Legal review is a human/governance gate**: E001's gating question is a legal\n151\t   decision (AGPL-3.0 redistribution and derivative-work posture) that AI tooling can\n152\t   support with research but cannot resolve; its investigation signals route it to a\n153\t   person. Turnaround is outside engineering control.\n154\t4. **Stranded-work risk**: E003/E004 (defaults) are intentionally not gated by E001\n155\t   because the strategy marks the SeaweedFS fallback as acceptable, so a bundled store\n156\t   ships in every bounded outcome. If both candidates were ultimately unshippable, the\n157\t   defaults work would be stranded — accepted risk, flagged for the reviewer.\n158\t5. **Dashboard ambiguity**: see Component Mapping Notes — passive classification is an\n159\t   interpretation; if the strategy author intended a Dashboard configuration/status\n160\t   surface for the bundled store, a Dashboard epic should be added.\n161\t\n162\t## Triage\n163\t\n164\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only): the strategy spans multiple\n165\tcomponents and architecturally distinct work streams (legal investigation, new-component\n166\tonboarding chain, operator enablement, per-component defaults, substantive documentation\n167\tauthoring), and contains a genuine unknown (AGPL clearance) that changes which epics exist.\n168\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"36177664-5838-4201-809a-3bbb0cba7d03","timestamp":"2026-10-22T1