{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a43ea653b7e10696","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E004\n3\ttitle: Model serving storage defaults for the bundled store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Model Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: -1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Model serving storage defaults for the bundled store\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMake model serving storage connections target the bundled S3-compatible object store\n34\tby default when it is enabled, so that model serving on disconnected clusters can\n35\tretrieve models and write serving-related artifacts without manual endpoint\n36\tconfiguration or customer-provided S3.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Default storage/connection configuration for model serving (model artifact retrieval\n41\t  and related storage) so that, when the bundled store is enabled on a cluster, serving\n42\t  resources use it without administrators hand-configuring endpoints.\n43\t- Explicitly configured customer-provided storage continues to take precedence over the\n44\t  bundled-store default (no regression for connected environments).\n45\t- Coordination contract: the default resolves the bundled store's endpoint through the\n46\t  convention established by the Platform Operator enablement capability (an endpoint\n47\t  reference, not a build-time artifact).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- On a cluster where the bundled store is enabled, a serving resource can retrieve a\n52\t  stored model from the bundled store with zero manual endpoint or credential\n53\t  configuration.\n54\t- Where an administrator has explicitly configured customer-provided storage, that\n55\t  configuration is honored and the bundled-store default does not override it.\n56\t- The defaulting behavior is covered by automated tests.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-3 (P1): Data Science Pipelines and model serving connection defaults can target\n61\t  the bundled store without manual endpoint configuration (model serving portion).\n62\t\n63\t## Risks / Notes\n64\t\n65\t- The strategy names \"model serving\" in this requirement but lists no serving component\n66\t  in its Affected Components; this epic is mapped to the canonical Serving Runtimes\n67\t  component and the owning team should be confirmed with the strategy author.\n68\t- No architecture context file exists for the serving components; the serving-side\n69\t  storage-dependency assumption could not be validated against architecture context.\n70\t- The bundled-store endpoint is a configuration reference resolved at execution time;\n71\t  this work proceeds in parallel with the Platform Operator enablement capability and\n72\t  is gated by the acceptance criterion above rather than a hard ordering.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"ae5128ba-64f2-4ed8-9a0b-59f6572849a4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:32:32.730Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a43ea653b7e10696","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
