{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d1e6d84ec320c8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E005\n3\ttitle: Bundled object store documentation (enablement, sizing, support boundary)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Documentation\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E004\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 0\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 4\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Bundled object store documentation (enablement, sizing, support boundary)\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tAuthor the customer-facing documentation for the bundled S3-compatible object store:\n37\thow administrators enable it, how to size it for disconnected and PoC clusters, and\n38\twhere the supported/unsupported boundary lies versus customer-provided storage. The\n39\tdocumentation describes what was actually built and is written after the implementation\n40\twork completes.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\tContent outline (topics to be authored inside the Red Hat docs content process):\n45\t\n46\t- **Enablement guide**: enabling the bundled store through the Platform Operator on\n47\t  disconnected and PoC clusters, including the opt-in default, the disable/rollback\n48\t  path, and behavior across platform upgrades.\n49\t- **Sizing guidance**: resource sizing (storage capacity, memory, CPU) for the bundled\n50\t  store for representative disconnected/PoC workloads (pipeline artifacts and model\n51\t  serving storage).\n52\t- **Supported/unsupported boundary**: what is supported with the bundled store versus\n53\t  customer-provided storage — including the out-of-scope statements from the strategy\n54\t  (no replacement of customer-provided S3 in connected environments, no data migration\n55\t  tooling between stores).\n56\t- **Consumption defaults**: how Data Science Pipelines and model serving target the\n57\t  bundled store by default, and how to override with customer-provided storage.\n58\t- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance that have customer-visible effects\n59\t  (e.g. attribution or notice requirements).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Published documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the\n64\t  supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage, matching the topics\n65\t  in the Scope outline.\n66\t- The documentation accurately reflects the shipped implementation (which store is\n67\t  bundled, the enablement mechanism, the upgrade behavior) — technically reviewed\n68\t  against the implementation by the owning engineers.\n69\t- The boundary documentation explicitly states the strategy's out-of-scope items\n70\t  (customer-provided S3 in connected environments is not replaced; no data migration\n71\t  tooling between stores).\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the\n76\t  supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- The documented store identity (the cleared candidate vs the Apache-2.0 fallback)\n81\t  follows the legal clearance outcome; documentation drafting starts only after the\n82\t  implementation epics complete.\n83\t- Priority is derived from the strategy-level priority (Major → P1) per the\n84\t  docs-authoring priority exception, even though HLR-4 is P2.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac