image, so bundled stores\n50\t  stay supported and patched — the explicit gap left by today's ad hoc field installs.\n51\t- Incorporation of any remediations required by the license validation of the image's\n52\t  transitive dependencies, and of any conditions attached to the legal clearance.\n53\t- A pinned image digest consumable as a configuration reference by the Platform\n54\t  Operator packaging.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A productized MinIO container image builds from the midstream repository with the\n59\t  Konflux build pipeline green.\n60\t- The image's transitive-dependency license findings are resolved or documented as\n61\t  cleared.\n62\t- The upgrade policy is implemented: a new upstream MinIO release (including security\n63\t  patches) can be ingested into a new productized image through the standard pipeline.\n64\t- A pinned image digest of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n65\t  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n66\t  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n67\t- Any conditions attached to the legal clearance are satisfied by the shipped image.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n72\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n73\t  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, MinIO branch).\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- Depends on upstream MinIO release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing is\n78\t  tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n79\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects MinIO.\n80\t  If the AGPL terms cannot be satisfied, this work restarts against the Apache-2.0\n81\t  fallback (SeaweedFS).\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"