endations for any findings (dependency replacement, exclusion, or\n51\t  additional clearance) handed to the image productization work.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A license scan report exists covering SeaweedFS and the complete transitive\n56\t  dependency set of the productized store image.\n57\t- Every dependency in the shipped image is classified as policy-compliant, or has a\n58\t  documented remediation carried into the image productization work.\n59\t- Scan findings that require legal interpretation are escalated and tracked to\n60\t  resolution.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n65\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n66\t  (supported/productized-images portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- Findings requiring legal sign-off introduce a human review gate; the scan itself is\n71\t  automated, but interpretation of edge-case licenses is not.\n72\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects the\n73\t  Apache-2.0 fallback.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"b76b4094-4332-404f-b077-0923bd0f70ae","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:32:46.125Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9a14f69b1e30776","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
