ging consumes.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The SeaweedFS midstream repository is onboarded to Konflux with an application and\n54\t  component configuration.\n55\t- The build pipeline produces a container image for the store from the repository's\n56\t  container build definition.\n57\t- Standard pipeline checks (including vulnerability and license checks applicable to\n58\t  the component) run green on a build of the repository.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n63\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n64\t  (productized-images portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n65\t\n66\t## Risks / Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Requires the midstream repository to exist first; deliberately runs in parallel with\n69\t  the image productization work — the pipeline being green is an acceptance criterion\n70\t  there, not an ordering constraint.\n71\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome selects the\n72\t  Apache-2.0 fallback.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"7c759754-b3e0-4f5c-baf0-f4f58e038c42","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:32:49.634Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a834e7ceede5420f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
