{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fcbb9e0a2e3f7a3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Productized SeaweedFS container image with upgrade lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E006\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E007\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the AGPL candidate is cleared, this branch is not executed;\n18\t    MinIO image productization runs instead\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: -1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: -1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Low\n32\tai_implementability_score: -3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Productized SeaweedFS container image with upgrade lifecycle\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tProductize the SeaweedFS container image for bundling: a supported, rebuildable image\n40\tbuilt from the midstream repository through Konflux, with the version/upgrade policy\n41\tthat the Platform Operator's upgrade lifecycle relies on. This work is conditional on\n42\tthe legal clearance outcome selecting the Apache-2.0 fallback as the bundled store.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Container image productization for the store: build hardening, image configuration\n47\t  (including the S3-compatible server configuration used for the bundled deployment),\n48\t  and version pinning aligned with the selected upstream version.\n49\t- Upgrade lifecycle support: a defined policy for tracking and ingesting upstream\n50\t  SeaweedFS releases (including security patches) into the productized image, so\n51\t  bundled stores stay supported and patched — the explicit gap left by today's ad hoc\n52\t  field installs.\n53\t- Incorporation of any remediations required by the license validation of the image's\n54\t  transitive dependencies.\n55\t- A pinned image digest consumable as a configuration reference by the Platform\n56\t  Operator packaging.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A productized SeaweedFS container image builds from the midstream repository with the\n61\t  Konflux build pipeline green.\n62\t- The image's transitive-dependency license findings are resolved or documented as\n63\t  cleared.\n64\t- The upgrade policy is implemented: a new upstream SeaweedFS release (including\n65\t  security patches) can be ingested into a new productized image through the standard\n66\t  pipeline.\n67\t- A pinned image digest of the productized image is published for consumption by the\n68\t  Platform Operator packaging (a configuration reference — no ordering constraint on\n69\t  the operator enablement work, which runs in parallel).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store\n74\t  through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle\n75\t  (productized images and upgrade lifecycle portion, SeaweedFS fallback branch).\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Depends on upstream SeaweedFS release cadence for security patches; ingestion timing\n80\t  is tracked as an ongoing operational concern, not a one-time deliverable.\n81\t- SeaweedFS is a less-proven fallback than the original candidate; functional\n82\t  validation of the S3-compatible surface against Data Science Pipelines and model\n83\t  serving workloads is folded into the acceptance criteria of the consuming epics.\n84\t- Conditional branch epic: executed only if the legal clearance outcome rejects the\n85\t  AGPL candidate.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ead96361a62f7d","agent_id":"ac3a1fa7a376e79fa","session_id":"44316181-c1df-4de5-a431-6d099bdfeb64","uuid":"6f53343c-ffd1-4e6e-9f30-3b4cad0999d6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:32:50.410Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fcbb9e0a2e3f7a3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
